    .btn-group.btn-group-sm(role="group",aria-label="Commands").mt-1
      
      button.btn.btn-primary(type="button",data-bs-toggle="collapse",data-bs-target="#talk-aedcf7788ad088602181f11ad8be720b",aria-expanded="false",aria-controls="talk-aedcf7788ad088602181f11ad8be720b")
        | #[i.bi.bi-file-earmark-text-fill] Abstract
      a(href="slides/Digital Accessibility in the AI era_ Promise, Pitfalls, and Progress.pdf",target="_blank").btn.btn-primary
        | #[i.bi.bi-easel3-fill] Slides
  .col-md-7
    p.abstract#talk-aedcf7788ad088602181f11ad8be720b.collapse.mt-2
        | This presentation offers a concise journey through the digital accessibility landscape. It opens by defining digital accessibility and its importance for ensuring equal participation for people with disabilities, before outlining the key regulatory and technical frameworks shaping practice today, including WCAG, the European Accessibility Act, and W3C standards. We then compare traditional pre-AI evaluation tools with emerging AI-powered approaches, examining how these new techniques show strong potential but currently face clear limitations. The presentation closes with a comparative human-AI case study on alternative text assessment and generation, using this example as a lens to examine the broader interplay between large-scale automation, quality, and human preferences.
