    p.abstract#talk-00cf9d350c414bb1d0ad2fbb6ff62e3b.collapse.mt-2
        | This talk explores the challenges posed by integrating Machine Learning (ML) into the field of Combinatorial Optimization (CO). Starting from the analysis of classic problems such as the Vehicle Routing Problem (VRP) and the Crew Scheduling Problem (CSP), the Column Generation (CG) algorithm will be presented as an effective solution methodology. After outlining the theoretical foundations and reviewing the state-of-the-art at the intersection of ML and CO, the presentation will focus on how predictive models can accelerate execution times and improve solution quality, aiming to stimulate a discussion on future research directions.
